        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Old oil in concrete is a depth problem, not a scrubbing problem. Clean the surface first to see what remains, then pick a method that reaches below it: a covered poultice for stains you want gone this week, an enzyme cleaner for large, faded patches you can leave alone for a while, and heat to make either one work faster.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Judge every round on dry concrete, repeat while it keeps improving, and stop when the stain no longer feels slick and water soaks in evenly. Then seal or coat the slab and fix the leak, so the work you just did lasts.
          </p>
        </div>

